WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.140
How does a neuron keep its own branches from tangling, while still overlapping its

2
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.140
neighbours?

3
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:11.053
Take one neuron's arbor.

4
00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:15.333
Its branches often spread evenly, without crossing or bundling.

5
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:17.893
This is self-avoidance.

6
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.593
Sister branches from the same cell touch, then move apart.

7
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:29.403
Yet fly sensory neurons share the body wall with other classes, and their dendrites

8
00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:30.403
overlap.

9
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:35.143
At every contact, a branch must ask: is this me, or someone else?

10
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:42.083
Predict. A protein binds only identical copies, and binding makes branches pull

11
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.223
apart. What must it be like?

12
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:55.273
Every branch of one neuron must carry the same version, so sister branches always

13
00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:56.273
match.

14
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:01.187
Neighbouring neurons must carry different versions, so their branches seldom match.

15
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.560
The fly has such a protein, from one gene, Dscam1.

16
00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.780
It comes in many isoforms.

17
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.000
Exons are the stretches of a gene kept in its messenger RNA.

18
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.500
Four of Dscam1's exons come as clusters of alternatives.

19
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.160
Each messenger RNA keeps one exon from each cluster.

20
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:33.460
That gives 19,008 outer surfaces, and 38,016 isoforms in all.

21
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:38.833
The fourth cluster builds the stretch that crosses the membrane, so it does not

22
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:40.053
change the outer surface.

23
00:01:41.116 --> 00:01:45.036
Each isoform binds mainly to identical isoforms.

24
00:01:45.056 --> 00:01:46.636
But matched branches pull apart.

25
00:01:47.656 --> 00:01:48.656
Same means retreat.

26
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.390
Remove Dscam1, and a neuron's own branches cross and bundle.

27
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.900
Take a neuron that lacks Dscam1 and give it a single isoform, and its own branches

28
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:00.900
spread apart again.

29
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.060
Predict. Now give every neuron the same single isoform.

30
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.060
What happens between neighbours?

31
00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.100
Neighbours that carry the same single isoform cannot tell themselves from each

32
00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.140
other. The logic predicts they avoid each other.

33
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:28.300
Flies whose Dscam1 could make only one outer surface had severely disorganised

34
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.300
circuits.

35
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.720
Which isoform a neuron carries matters little.

36
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.660
Differing from its neighbours is what matters.

37
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:44.343
Why thousands? Picture each neuron drawing about twenty badges from a bowl.

38
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:48.373
From a small bowl, a neighbour carries many of your badges.

39
00:02:49.433 --> 00:02:52.193
From a huge bowl, a neighbour carries almost none.

40
00:02:53.166 --> 00:02:57.686
In the huge bowl, sister branches match completely and a neighbour only slightly.

41
00:02:58.786 --> 00:03:01.486
Flies need thousands of isoforms to wire normally.

42
00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.790
Mouse DSCAM is not spliced this way.

43
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:11.740
Instead, starburst amacrine cells use gamma protocadherins, adhesion proteins of the

44
00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:16.240
cadherin family. Without them, each cell's own dendrites cross and clump.

45
00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:22.073
In starburst cells lacking the protocadherins, give every cell the same single

46
00:03:22.073 --> 00:03:26.493
isoform. Each arbor separates, but neighbours avoid each other too.

47
00:03:27.466 --> 00:03:32.326
With only about 58 genes, recognition is thought to compare the whole combination,

48
00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.226
not single isoforms.

49
00:03:35.266 --> 00:03:40.266
Takeaway: a label unique to one cell, read as retreat, keeps that cell's own

50
00:03:40.266 --> 00:03:41.026
branches apart.
